From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:12:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pci: samsung,exynos9820-pcie: Add the endpoint
 supply

The Wi-Fi chip of the Galaxy S10+ sits on this controller and only answers
once its Wi-Fi half is powered up by a GPIO line.  The vendor driver raises
that line and waits 100 ms before it lets the controller train the link,
so the controller needs a supply it can switch on before it releases the
endpoint from reset.

Describe it the way the other DesignWare hosts do, as vpcie3v3-supply.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/pci/samsung,exynos9820-pcie.yaml    | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/samsung,exynos9820-pcie.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/samsung,exynos9820-pcie.yaml
index cd97f935988..ff208323697 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/samsung,exynos9820-pcie.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/samsung,exynos9820-pcie.yaml
@@ -69,6 +69,12 @@ properties:
       The line that holds the endpoint in reset, released once the controller
       is ready to train the link.
 
+  vpcie3v3-supply:
+    description:
+      Supply of the endpoint, switched on while the endpoint is still held in
+      reset.  On boards with the Wi-Fi chip soldered on, it is the line that
+      powers the Wi-Fi half of that chip up.
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
